+/* On Android the kernel has no /dev/ntsync device, so get_inproc_device_fd()
+ * calls ntsync_init() (from the userspace ntsync-android library) and returns
+ * the NTSYNC_ANDROID_USED_BY_SERVER sentinel. All subsequent ioctl() calls
+ * in this file are replaced by direct ntsync_* function calls. Object "fds"
+ * stored in struct inproc_sync.fd are actually u32 ntsync-android handles. */
 
